My assumption was that racketeers are burning through many early 
characters relatively quickly, so that the ascension:playing time rate 
should be high, even if ascension:number of starting characters is low.

(Alternatively, based on some claims I've read, the player is so good at 
playing the racket that he does *not* burn many starting characters, 
which would mean that even if the early game is done rather slowly, the 
ascension:playing time rate should still be high.)

But your assessment is probably correct: the AC boost from doing the 
racket is simply not that great an advantage. AC is only one component 
of a survivable character, others being HP, luck, and intrinsics, some 
of which are difficult to get while playing pacifist, especially in the 
early game. ("Darn! My pet ate my elf corpse. Rats! My pet ate my 
floating eye corpse. Oy! My pet killed the unicorn I was going to chuck 
gems at, and ate the corpse....") Which means that the risks of the 
racket are all the more not worth taking, because even when you 
successfully accomplish it, your character is still quite vulnerable.

